We have
\[
17_b=b+7,\qquad 97_b=9b+7.
\]
We need \(b+7\mid 9b+7\). Let \(d=b+7\). Then \(b=d-7\), so
\[
9b+7=9(d-7)+7=9d-56.
\]
Thus \(d\mid 56\). Since \(b>9\), we have \(d=b+7>16\). The positive divisors of \(56\) greater than \(16\) are \(28\) and \(56\). Therefore
\[
b=28-7=21,\qquad b=56-7=49.
\]
Their sum is
\[
21+49=70.
\]

